1
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:07,020
Wealth. Fame. Power. Gold Roger,

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:12,740
the King of the Pirates, obtained this and
everything else the world had to offer.

3
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:17,397
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:19,060
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:20,560
You can have it.

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:23,720
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

7
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,180
Now you just have to fire it.

8
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,917
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,797
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dare to imagine.

10
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:35,920
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

11
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,620
This is a small seaport village.

12
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,877
For the past year or so, a pirate
ship has been anchored at the port.

13
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:50,860
A soft wind from the east blows gently
over this peaceful, sleepy place.

14
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,960
Loopy, come on.

15
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,747
What are you doing up there?

16
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,677
I'm not kidding around, you hear me?

17
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,120
I'm really mad!

18
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,908
Watch, I'll prove it to ya!

19
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,040
Yeah, go ahead, kid.

20
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,968
Not sure what you're
planning to do, though.

21
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:12,560
You idiot!

22
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,253
What'd you do that for?

23
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,840
Alright, drink up! Cheers!

24
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:20,817
Let's drink to Luffy's courage and
our great journey on the theme!

25
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:21,730
Cheers!

26
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:25,420
Didn't hurt at all!

27
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,577
That's a lie if I've ever heard one.

28
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:28,760
I'm not lying!

29
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,797
And I'm not scared of
getting hurt again, either!

30
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,177
You gotta take me with
you on your next voyage!

31
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,080
I wanna be a pirate like you!

32
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,150
Hahaha!

33
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,017
Yeah, right, as if you
could ever be a pirate.

34
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,717
I don't think you're gonna fare too
well at sea if you sink like an anchor.

35
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,397
I'll be okay as long as
I don't fall overboard!

36
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,937
And besides, I'm a
really good fighter, too!

37
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:50,549
I've got lots of training!

38
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:53,537
I mean, when I punch people,
it's like firing a pistol!

39
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,450
A pistol?

40
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:55,837
If you say so.

41
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,900
Are you makin' fun of me?

42
00:01:58,980 --> 00:01:59,810
Hey!

43
00:01:59,893 --> 00:02:01,560
Don't be in such a sour mood, kiddo!

44
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,717
You're still young!

45
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,077
You should be having fun!

46
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:06,748
And being a pirate's
more fun than anything!

47
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:09,260
We get to travel across the endless sea!

48
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,617
Discovering new places all the time!

49
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,340
We're as free as can be!

50
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,977
I'd appreciate it if you clowns
didn't teach him that kind of thing.

51
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,860
But you know it's true, right?

52
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,040
Come on, boss!

53
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,597
We can take him on one little voyage!

54
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:23,577
What's the harm?

55
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:24,836
Yeah, he'll be okay!

56
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,140
Fine, but one of you gets left behind.

57
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:29,680
Yeah, forget that!

58
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:31,417
Let's get back to drinking!

59
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,040
Put you guys on my side!

60
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:36,237
I'm just saying, you're much too
young to try and strike out your seed.

61
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,217
You can ask me about it in ten
years and maybe I'll reconsider.

62
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,130
Stupid shakes!

63
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,516
I'm not that little!

64
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,020
Jeez, calm down.

65
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,574
Drink some juice, kid.

66
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,240
Yay, thank you!

67
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,997
Real pirates don't drink juice, big guy!

68
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,910
No, that's not fair!

69
00:02:50,993 --> 00:02:51,823
You tricked me!

70
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,200
Whatever, I'm tired now.

71
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:58,980
Luffy, you have to try to understand
how the boss feels. Mr. First Mate!

72
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:00,537
Think about it.

73
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:03,217
This guy is the captain of a
tough-as-nails pirate crew.

74
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:07,177
So he knows more than anybody how
dangerous this kind of life can be.

75
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,280
My point is,

76
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:12,097
he told you not to come along with us
because he didn't want to break your spirit.

77
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,157
You don't get it!

78
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:16,437
He's just making fun of me
because he thinks I'm a kid!

79
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,340
Hey, Anchor. You see?

80
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:20,600
You're having fun as always.

81
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:24,511
Yeah, I get such a kick out of
giving this kid a hard time.

82
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,280
Luffy, would you like
to order some food too?

83
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,704
Put it on my treasure tab, kay?

84
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,333
The treasure tab again?

85
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:34,540
You know, that does qualify
as stealing. Nuh-uh!

86
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,137
Once I become a pirate and
find a bunch of treasure,

87
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,197
I'm gonna pay back every last bit!

88
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,540
I know you will.

89
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,640
Shanks! Yeah? What?

90
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:47,237
How much longer are you gonna be here for?

91
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:48,340
I'm not too sure.

92
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,117
I believe the plan we decided on was to
go on a couple more voyages then head

93
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:58,160
out towards the north after we're done
with that only a couple more trips huh

94
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,317
okay then i can practice my swimming while

95
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,500
you're here that's a good
idea knock yourself out

96
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:17,660
excuse us so these are what pass for
pirates here looks awfully sad to me

97
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:30,777
you see we're mountain bandits
but we didn't come here

98
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:34,317
to tear your place apart we'll
just take some booze i'm so

99
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,197
sorry sir but we're actually
fresh out of alcohol for the

100
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:41,577
moment huh those pirates seem
to be drinking though is that

101
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:46,517
water no that was the last bit
of what i had stuck up well

102
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:49,557
this is a problem isn't it it
looks like my friends and i

103
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:53,977
drank the place dry before you
gentlemen came in sorry you

104
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:57,589
can have this one if you like
it hasn't even been opened yet

105
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:10,097
how dare you can you not see
who you're talking to you

106
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,957
know damn well that won't
even be enough for a nightcap

107
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:17,497
oh now the floor's all wet
and sticky look at this

108
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:20,780
pal i've got a bounty of 8
million berries on my head.

109
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:25,820
I've killed 56 people, and all of
them were mouthy fools like you.

110
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:28,141
If I were you, I'd watch my back.

111
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:33,177
But since we're in the mountains and you're
on the sea, maybe we won't meet again.

112
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:34,090
Huh?

113
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:36,665
Sorry about the mess, Machine.

114
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,140
Have you got a rag?

115
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,580
Oh, no, don't worry.

116
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,034
I can take care of it.

117
